  "answer": "Customer feedback on citation reliability shifted from being the top Q1 complaint to a largely resolved issue in Q2, though some residual pain points remain. In Q1, citation reliability was the single most prominent complaint, with users reporting incorrect file links (42%), missing page numbers (28%), empty citations (18%), and broken links (12%) [NL-010-S05][NL-010-S01]. In Q2, following the April 2026 deployment, citation accuracy tickets declined steadily (42 in April, 31 in May, 24 in June) [NL-011-S05]. Overall NPS rose from 41 to 44, driven by the April fix, with improved trust in regulated industries and BrightPath Healthcare restarting their pilot [NL-011-S01][NL-011-S03]. However, remaining citation tickets in May and June are almost entirely linked to scanned, image-only PDFs, which still lack OCR processing, plus a minor indexing lag during peak hours [NL-011-S05][NL-016-S04].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
